**/.terraform/
**/terraform.tfstate
**/terraform.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!infra/tfvars/*.tfvars
!infra/tfvars/*.tfvars.example
*.tfplan
.mise.toml
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.local/
e2e/artifacts/
# The browser bundle. It is one file now and it carries React, so a commit of it is a
# megabyte of generated code per UI change. Every path that needs it builds it:
# `pnpm build` runs before the tests in CI and inside the image, and the checks that
# read it refuse to pass when it is missing.
apps/automation-app/public/*.js
# The stylesheets are copied here by the same build. A committed copy is worse than no
# copy: `readAsset` prefers it over the source, so a stale one is served in a checkout
# nobody has built, which is a page styled by whatever the last person happened to commit.
apps/automation-app/public/styles/
